  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A Young's double slit interference arrangement with slits <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> is immersed in water (refractive index <math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> ) as shown in the figure. The positions of maxima on the surface of water are given by <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">λ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> , where <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">λ</mi></math> is the wavelength of light in air (refractive index = 1), <math><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></math> is the separation between the slits and m is an integer. The value of p is<br ><br/><img src=\"assets\\qt0010_fc7b05936a77.png\"/></p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "3",
  "solution": {
